{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The Lord showed me a [G]sight
A [D]basket of summer [Em]fruit
He asked what [G]I see, Amos
I [D]answered the Lord's [Em]truth
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The end has come for [G]Israel
[D]I will never pass them [Em]by
The time of grace is [G]finished
[D]Under the open [Em]sky
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Em] | [D] | [Em] | [D] |
| [Em] | [Em] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
On that day the palace [G]sings
But [D]the song turns to [Em]wailing
The temple songs are bro[G]ken
[D]The joy is [Em]now failing
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[C]Corpses ev[G]erywhere are found
[D]Flung out in silence [Em]deep
[C]No one [G]hears the lament
[D]As the secrets sleep
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Em]The end has come for [G]Israel
The [D]basket holds the [Em]day
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
